LCMC agreed in September to lease the hospital for at least 45 years. The deal also included paying the parish $200 million in rental fees and more than $300 million in capital improvements.
"Many of the areas of concern are rooted in the failure to select, or alternatively establish, proper foundations for the core front-end process," McClintock said.
He said the decision for his office to monitor the negotiation process was based on the unique and complex nature of mergers and acquisitions and the long-term impact on health care services in Jefferson Parish.
The West Jefferson Medical Center lease is valued at approximately $563 million.
McClintock said his office found issues related to accountability, transparency and waste within government throughout the transaction. He said the parish spent nearly $4 million for consultant services that were not consistent or compliant with parish ordinances or the West Jefferson Medical Center process.
