NYS Fair, Syracuse- The weather for the first Friday of the 2017 New York State Fair is looking nice.
A small disturbance is passing by the region this morning with some extra cloud cover. A brief, very light shower may also be possible, though most areas will remain dry.
By later this morning, fair weather clouds will start to develop. The sun will be in and out of these clouds through the afternoon. The chance for a brief, light shower will remain but will be very low.
Skies should clear this evening as the sun begins to set.
Temperatures will continue to run well below normal for late August.
Morning temperatures will slowly rise from the upper 50s into the 60s. Afternoon highs will top out just shy of 70 degrees.
With clearing skies this evening, the temperature should drop rather quickly. By the time the Fair closes for the night, expect temperatures to be back into the upper 50s.
Winds today will remain light throughout the entire day. Calm winds are expected this evening.
