Sports Direct missed its earnings target for the year and underlying profit dropped 8.4%, as political and media pressure on the discount sports retailer made trading difficult.
But shares are surging on Thursday morning after the company unveiled strong profit growth and solid revenue growth.
Here are the key facts and figures from Sports Direct's preliminary results, released on Thursday:
Revenue up 2.5% to £2.9 billion;
Underlying earning before interest, tax, and other costs down 0.5% to £381.4 million;
