This week in food. Briefly:
BURGERS, BOURBON & BEER BENEFIT: Sunday from 4-7 p.m. at Generations Hall is a Burgers, Bourbon & Beer competition among nine top local burger shops to benefit Second Harvest Food Bank. Sponsored by Glazer's, the event will feature sliders paired with specialty bourbon cocktails or beer. Participating restaurants will compete for the "Best Burger" title, decided by a panel of judges; event-goers will vote for a "People's Choice" award. Competing restaurants include Bourbon House, Cheeseburger Eddie's, Company Burger, Cowbell, Phil's Grill, Rock-N-Bowl/Straight Stick Ranch, Sylvain, Tru Burger and Vitascope Hall. La Divina Gelateria is providing a special gelato. Tickets are $35 in advance online at www.no-hunger.org or in person at Second Harvest Food Bank, 700 Edwards Ave. in the Elmwood area. If available, tickets at the door will be $45.
********
PANERA BREAD FUNDRAISER IN COVINGTON: The first Covington location of Panera Bread, 70411 Hwy. 21, will have a tasting event Saturday to benefit Second Harvest Food Bank. "A Taste of Panera" tickets are $15 and admit two people for one hour, from either 11:30 a.m.-12:30 p.m. or noon-1 p.m., to sample menu selections. Limited tickets are available at www.no-hunger.org or buy them at the food bank, 700 Edwards Ave., Monday through Friday between 8 a.m. and 4 p.m.
********
WAITING AROUND EVEN LONGER: "Waiting Around (the Restaurant Musical)," the show that depicts life in the restaurant industry, is being held over through Sept. 24 at The Allways Lounge and Theatre. Showtime is 8 p.m. Mondays. Now in its 10th year, the show has had more than 200 performances, including New Orleans and New York runs. Featured are Tracey E. Collins, Jason Kirkpatrick, Darcy Malone, and Chris Wecklein, with composer Harry Mayronne at the piano. Book and lyrics are by Ricky Graham. Direction and choreography are by Amanda Zirkenbach. Buy tickets, $20, at the show's website, www.WaitingAroundTheMusical.com, or at the box office, 2240 St. Claude Ave., after 7:15 p.m. Mondays.
********
